1
00:00:08,628 --> 00:00:12,234
Divide mind from matter, and
the gap can never be bridged.

2
00:00:12,314 --> 00:00:15,459
Reach for a cup, and
no gap is ever crossed.

3
00:00:16,264 --> 00:00:18,892
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:18,972 --> 00:00:22,850
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:26,777
Part 1 set out the habit that
there has to be something.

6
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:31,737
Part 2 took it to the hard problem, and
showed a gap made by two fixed natures.

7
00:00:31,817 --> 00:00:36,125
Here I want to set two pictures
side by side. The gap we drew.

8
00:00:36,205 --> 00:00:38,874
And the living fact we
never stopped living.

9
00:00:39,672 --> 00:00:42,816
On paper, mind and matter cannot meet.

10
00:00:42,896 --> 00:00:45,226
In life, they never once fail to.

11
00:00:46,036 --> 00:00:48,216
First, a useful division.

12
00:00:49,016 --> 00:00:51,712
Dividing mind from matter is not foolish.

13
00:00:51,792 --> 00:00:54,321
It is one of the most useful cuts we make.

14
00:00:54,401 --> 00:00:57,989
The doctor asks whether a pain
is in the knee, or in the head.

15
00:00:58,069 --> 00:01:02,215
The neurologist separates what a scan
shows from what the patient reports.

16
00:01:02,295 --> 00:01:05,095
The law separates what you
did from what you intended.

17
00:01:05,175 --> 00:01:08,370
In ordinary speech, I
say I changed my mind,

18
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:11,486
and I moved the table,
and everyone understands.

19
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,105
Each of these works,
within its own agreements.

20
00:01:15,185 --> 00:01:17,768
As a convention, the division is fine.

21
00:01:17,848 --> 00:01:20,580
It singles out two
aspects of what appears,

22
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:24,172
so that we can talk,
treat, measure and judge.

23
00:01:24,976 --> 00:01:28,623
The trouble begins when the
convention is taken for two things.

24
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:32,891
Mind becomes an inner stuff,
whose nature is to be felt.

25
00:01:32,971 --> 00:01:36,695
Matter becomes an outer stuff,
whose nature is to lack feeling.

26
00:01:36,775 --> 00:01:39,276
Each is now complete on its own side.

27
00:01:39,356 --> 00:01:43,724
And then every ordinary event turns
into a puzzle that cannot be solved.

28
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,156
How does a thought move an arm?

29
00:01:46,236 --> 00:01:48,602
How does light on the
eye become a seen colour?

30
00:01:48,682 --> 00:01:53,063
How does coffee make me alert, or
a sad memory make my chest heavy?

31
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:57,833
Asked between two fixed natures,
each of these needs a bridge.

32
00:01:57,913 --> 00:01:59,627
And no bridge can be built.

33
00:01:59,707 --> 00:02:02,969
That is the gap of Part
2. It is unbridgeable.

34
00:02:03,049 --> 00:02:05,840
But only because we made
the two banks first.

35
00:02:06,656 --> 00:02:10,113
Now drop the picture, and
look at what actually happens.

36
00:02:10,932 --> 00:02:13,479
I want a drink. My hand reaches.

37
00:02:13,559 --> 00:02:15,598
My fingers close around the cup.

38
00:02:15,678 --> 00:02:17,663
I feel its warmth and weight.

39
00:02:17,743 --> 00:02:19,733
I lift it, and I drink.

40
00:02:20,536 --> 00:02:24,632
At no point is there a moment when a
thought has to travel over to a hand.

41
00:02:24,712 --> 00:02:26,411
Nothing is sent across.

42
00:02:26,491 --> 00:02:30,053
Wanting, seeing, reaching,
feeling the weight.

43
00:02:30,133 --> 00:02:32,702
They arise together, each with the others,

44
00:02:32,782 --> 00:02:34,527
in one seamless movement.

45
00:02:35,324 --> 00:02:37,314
It is the same everywhere I look.

46
00:02:38,112 --> 00:02:40,006
A door slams behind me.

47
00:02:40,086 --> 00:02:43,743
The sound, the jump, the
racing heart are one event.

48
00:02:43,823 --> 00:02:46,936
I do not first hear, then
decide to be startled,

49
00:02:47,016 --> 00:02:48,965
then send the order to my body.

50
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:52,979
I walk over uneven ground,
talking all the while.

51
00:02:53,059 --> 00:02:56,516
The feet find the stones without
any instructions from me.

52
00:02:57,320 --> 00:03:00,125
I drink coffee, and the dullness lifts.

53
00:03:00,205 --> 00:03:03,291
A sad memory comes, and
the chest grows heavy.

54
00:03:03,371 --> 00:03:07,656
The mental and the physical are never
found waiting on opposite banks.

55
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:09,906
And it is effortless.

56
00:03:09,986 --> 00:03:13,303
No one has ever had to work at
joining their mind to their body.

57
00:03:13,383 --> 00:03:16,129
We have never once felt
a bridge being crossed.

58
00:03:16,209 --> 00:03:18,928
The interaction is simply how living goes.

59
00:03:19,008 --> 00:03:21,840
It is a living fact. Not a theory.

60
00:03:22,648 --> 00:03:26,350
So the order is the other way
round from how we usually think.

61
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:29,638
The seamless interaction
comes first, as lived.

62
00:03:29,718 --> 00:03:33,039
The gap comes afterwards,
as a picture laid over it.

63
00:03:33,836 --> 00:03:38,529
Why is it seamless? Not because mind
and matter are secretly one stuff.

64
00:03:38,609 --> 00:03:41,115
Because neither has a nature of its own.

65
00:03:41,928 --> 00:03:46,223
Almost every way of thinking about
relation tries to settle it by collapsing

66
00:03:46,303 --> 00:03:47,885
one side into the other.

67
00:03:47,965 --> 00:03:51,200
Reductionism collapses
the whole into its parts.

68
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:54,081
Holism collapses the parts into a Whole.

69
00:03:54,161 --> 00:03:56,839
Materialism collapses mind into matter.

70
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:59,638
Idealism collapses matter into mind.

71
00:03:59,718 --> 00:04:03,197
And a ground, energy,
a field, or awareness,

72
00:04:03,277 --> 00:04:05,702
collapses both into a third stuff.

73
00:04:06,508 --> 00:04:09,132
Each one needs one side to be really real,

74
00:04:09,212 --> 00:04:11,595
so that the relation
has somewhere to rest.

75
00:04:12,392 --> 00:04:16,592
Dependent arising and emptiness give
another way of understanding relation,

76
00:04:16,672 --> 00:04:18,539
connection and interaction.

77
00:04:18,619 --> 00:04:21,152
Without the need to
resolve one into the other.

78
00:04:21,948 --> 00:04:23,856
The intending and the moving.

79
00:04:23,936 --> 00:04:25,921
The light and the seen colour.

80
00:04:26,001 --> 00:04:28,163
The key and the opening door.

81
00:04:28,243 --> 00:04:31,533
Each arises with the other,
and neither is the floor.

82
00:04:31,613 --> 00:04:36,007
Nothing has to be reduced, because
nothing had a nature to be reduced to.

83
00:04:36,808 --> 00:04:39,491
And the relation is not
a third thing either.

84
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:43,811
Relation is what is really real,
would only be one more ground.

85
00:04:43,891 --> 00:04:46,737
The relating is as empty
as what it relates.

86
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:49,489
Seamless does not mean merged.

87
00:04:49,569 --> 00:04:52,505
Sound stays sound, and
colour stays colour.

88
00:04:52,585 --> 00:04:55,005
The warmth of the cup is not the wanting.

89
00:04:55,085 --> 00:04:57,492
Distinctions stay perfectly vivid.

90
00:04:57,572 --> 00:05:01,445
What goes is only their standing
apart, each on its own side,

91
00:05:01,525 --> 00:05:02,931
needing to be joined.

92
00:05:03,744 --> 00:05:08,623
In a world without a substrate, this is
understood in a way very close to Mipham's

93
00:05:08,703 --> 00:05:10,924
two models of the two truths.

94
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:15,614
Mipham, the great Nyingma scholar
of the nineteenth century,

95
00:05:15,694 --> 00:05:18,227
presented the two truths in two ways.

96
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:22,262
In the first, the conventional
truth is appearance,

97
00:05:22,342 --> 00:05:26,315
and the ultimate truth is emptiness,
and the two are inseparable.

98
00:05:26,395 --> 00:05:29,186
This is the Middle Way's
account of how things are.

99
00:05:29,988 --> 00:05:34,161
In the second, the two truths are told
apart by whether experience accords with

100
00:05:34,241 --> 00:05:39,573
how things are. Experience that accords,
non-dual, and without reification,

101
00:05:39,653 --> 00:05:41,366
is on the side of the ultimate.

102
00:05:41,446 --> 00:05:45,198
Experience that does not
accord, dualistic and reifying,

103
00:05:45,278 --> 00:05:47,023
is on the side of the relative.

104
00:05:47,824 --> 00:05:50,248
The substrateless view meets both.

105
00:05:51,068 --> 00:05:55,164
Ontologically, the two truths are
emptiness and dependent arising.

106
00:05:55,244 --> 00:05:57,256
Not two facts, but one.

107
00:05:57,336 --> 00:05:59,566
What arises dependently is empty.

108
00:05:59,646 --> 00:06:01,866
And being empty, it arises.

109
00:06:02,664 --> 00:06:05,410
Experientially, it is
a non-substantialist,

110
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:11,171
non-dual experience, against a reified,
dualistic taste of action and agency,

111
00:06:11,251 --> 00:06:13,974
of an object and its characteristics.

112
00:06:14,788 --> 00:06:18,109
That reified taste is what
Part 1 called the habit.

113
00:06:18,189 --> 00:06:22,375
A flash happens, and the habit
supplies the lightning that flashes.

114
00:06:22,455 --> 00:06:27,212
A reaching happens, and the habit supplies
a mind over here that sends orders to a

115
00:06:27,292 --> 00:06:28,517
hand over there.

116
00:06:28,597 --> 00:06:33,028
When the habit is seen through, the
same reaching is tasted as it is lived.

117
00:06:33,108 --> 00:06:35,419
Seamless. Without effort.

118
00:06:35,499 --> 00:06:37,375
No one standing behind it.

119
00:06:37,455 --> 00:06:39,092
Nothing crossing over.

120
00:06:39,896 --> 00:06:42,415
One caution, and here I am careful.

121
00:06:42,495 --> 00:06:46,899
Some readers worry that the second model
can make the authentic experience sound

122
00:06:46,979 --> 00:06:48,570
like a positive ground.

123
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:51,709
A pure awareness that is
finally, really there.

124
00:06:51,789 --> 00:06:53,462
I do not take it that way.

125
00:06:53,542 --> 00:06:57,483
The non-dual taste is itself
dependently arisen, and empty.

126
00:06:57,563 --> 00:07:01,424
It is not a new floor, laid
where the old one was taken away.

127
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:06,030
Otherwise the experiential side slides
straight back into a presence standing

128
00:07:06,110 --> 00:07:09,363
behind things, and the
whole problem returns.

129
00:07:10,164 --> 00:07:12,969
This can be noticed in
any ordinary moment.

130
00:07:13,768 --> 00:07:18,067
Pick up a cup. Look for the point where
the wanting hands over to the hand.

131
00:07:18,147 --> 00:07:19,784
There is no such point.

132
00:07:20,588 --> 00:07:24,792
When startled, notice how sound,
jump and heartbeat come as one.

133
00:07:25,608 --> 00:07:28,802
And when the thought comes,
my mind is moving my body,

134
00:07:28,882 --> 00:07:32,013
see that it comes afterwards.
As one more thought.

135
00:07:32,093 --> 00:07:34,925
A picture of the event. Not the event.

136
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:37,512
The convention stays useful.

137
00:07:37,592 --> 00:07:40,053
The doctor still asks where it hurts.

138
00:07:40,133 --> 00:07:44,115
What drops away is only the belief
that the convention is two things,

139
00:07:44,195 --> 00:07:45,519
needing a bridge.

140
00:07:46,328 --> 00:07:50,243
This is Section 3, Part 3 of
the Dependent Arising series,

141
00:07:50,323 --> 00:07:52,204
and the close of Section 3.

142
00:07:53,004 --> 00:07:56,013
On paper, the gap could never be bridged.

143
00:07:56,093 --> 00:07:58,775
In life, it was never there to cross.

